    "summary": "High‑energy Baltimore ’82 with monster second set & stellar matrix mix",
    "review": "April 19, 1982 at the Baltimore Civic Center is one of those early‑’80s shows that still feels fresh. The band rides a high‑octane wave through the second set – think Raven Space soaring into an inspired Feel Like A Stranger → Franklin’s Tower → Estimated Prophet → Terrapin Station suite, then a seamless Wheel → Truckin' → Stella Blue → Around & Around cascade that still makes you grin. Jerry’s voice shines on Peggy‑O and his guitar wails on Stella Blue and They Love Each Other; Phil lays down “more nitrous” bass that lifts the jams, while Brent Mydland is in high gear with crisp, soaring keys. The encore’s Brokedown Palace wraps the night with a heartfelt, lingering moment.\n\nFor listeners, the Kevin Tobin matrix (≈60 % soundboard/40 % audience) is the clear winner – it captures the band’s insanity with sweet, balanced clarity and avoids the thin low‑end that haunts many ’82 SBD tapes. The audience tape by Martin Warner also shines if you prefer a warm, crowd‑filled vibe, but nothing matches the matrix’s detail and punch.\n\nOverall, this concert is a solid 4‑star outing: the setlist flows beautifully, the energy never dips, and the recording options let both audiophiles and tape‑collectors enjoy the magic.",
